ers, I likely have the best hand. A small value bet of 100-300 chips can extract value from weaker Aces (with worse kickers), pocket pairs like KK-22, or missed draws. If opponent has a straight or flush, they likely would have bet earlier. Checking back misses value extraction opportunity, while betting too much risks only getting called by better hands. A modest bet of 200 chips represents good value while minimizing risk.\n\nAnswer: 200"}
